# D53 NEG — RECEIVER-SHAPE axis: `self.<field>` receiver inside an `equip`
# method. The sibling of the free-function field receiver; the axis is the
# RECEIVER, not the function kind.
# CELL: lock=Mutex · position=push · receiver=self.field · source=named local.
# The local is bound from a fresh TEMP (`Mutex[int](7)`), which D53 keeps POS at
# the bind — so the ONLY thing this fixture can reject on is the push, and it
# cannot go green for the bind-position reason.
# RED at 3c3ea3f0b: `gg check` ACCEPTED.
# ggdef: ABSTAIN (Mutex out of subset; owner: ggdef stays simple).

struct Holder:
    Vector[Mutex[int]] locks

equip Holder:
    void stash(&self):
        Mutex[int] m = Mutex[int](7)
        self.locks.push(m)

void main():
    Holder h = Holder([])
    print(h.locks.len())
